
### merge asks GitHub to merge the current branch's pull request, and returns
$ git stack merge
asked GitHub to merge #2 (feat-b) with the 1 below it: pending
it merges in the background; run 'git stack sync' to take in the result
[exit 0]
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}
GET repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls head=octo:feat-b state=open
PUT repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/2/merge-async sha=57c79b009bfdeb9790497f3ee09e4ed3a2562a61

### merge refuses while a branch up to here has unpushed commits
$ git stack merge
error: 'feat-a' has commits git-stack has not pushed; run 'git stack submit' first
[exit 1]

### merge reports GitHub refusing it
$ git stack merge
error: GitHub refused to merge #2: Required status check "ci" is failing
[exit 1]

### merge needs a github stack and a pull request
$ git stack merge
error: 'git stack merge' needs a github stack; merge on your hosting service, then run 'git stack sync'
[exit 1]
$ git stack merge
error: 'feat-c' has commits git-stack has not pushed; run 'git stack submit' first
[exit 1]

### sync takes in a merge: drops the merged branch, follows GitHub's rebase
$ git stack sync
fetching origin
syncing stack rooted at feat-a
'feat-a': #1 merged; dropped it from the stack (the branch is kept; 'git branch -D feat-a' removes it)
'feat-b': took in origin/feat-b as GitHub left it
done.
[exit 0]
feat-a parent (dropped): none
feat-a still a branch: yes
feat-b parent: main
feat-b == origin/feat-b: yes
feat-b stackPushed == tip: yes
feat-b base == origin/main: yes
$ git stack tree
  main (trunk, restacks onto origin/main)
  * feat-b (1 commit(s)) [github]
[exit 0]

### sync leaves a branch with unpushed commits, and the branches above it
$ git stack sync
fetching origin
syncing stack rooted at feat-a
'feat-a': #1 merged; dropped it from the stack (the branch is kept; 'git branch -D feat-a' removes it)
warning: skipping 'feat-b': it has commits not on 'origin/feat-b'; run 'git stack submit' to push them, or reset it to 'origin/feat-b'
warning: skipping 'feat-c': its parent 'feat-b' was skipped
error: sync skipped 2 branch(es): feat-b, feat-c
Deal with the branches warned about above, then re-run 'git stack sync'.
[exit 1]
feat-b behind origin/feat-b: 2
feat-c parent: feat-b

### sync moves a branch checked out in another worktree from there
$ git stack sync
fetching origin
syncing stack rooted at feat-a
'feat-a': #1 merged; dropped it from the stack (the branch is kept; 'git branch -D feat-a' removes it)
'feat-b': took in origin/feat-b as GitHub left it
done.
[exit 0]
worktree HEAD == origin/feat-b: yes

### sync does not restack a github stack onto a trunk that moved
$ git stack sync
fetching origin
syncing stack rooted at feat-a
done.
[exit 0]
feat-a behind main: 1
